WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
In just three months at the end of 2024,

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.360
the UK bought 59.5 billion pounds
more goods from the world than it

3
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.500
sold. Services, like
finance and business advice,

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.430
earned 49.3 billion back.

5
00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:19.060
Income and transfers paid
abroad took a little more away.

6
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:24.530
Overall, the current account came
up 18.7 billion pounds short.

7
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:27.940
So when a country buys more
from the world than it sells,

8
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.050
how does it pay the difference?

9
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:34.000
In this mission, you'll build a country's
accounts from credits and debits,

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.440
line by line.

11
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.000
Then you'll see why every
transaction is written down twice,

12
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.300
and what the second entry tells you.

13
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.250
Your mission: find out
how a country covers what

14
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.290
it cannot pay from its earnings.
